@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Current-season canonical production coverage — build 2233
+
+## Evidence and reproduced causes
+
+Baseline: v1.22.17/build 2232, commit 500d985d2f31c97680370a616a9303c47d60ca7f, tree d2d7ff68b22b855f9bd822400031a350ae6952e7. Main Chat supplied an authenticated Granite observation for player:4984: missing canonical fantasy windows despite separate roster Career History Weeks 1–8 / 183.82 points. This session did not reproduce the private request. That roster total is neither the canonical target nor a substitute.
+
+Deterministic canonical-store fixtures establish four shared losses: individual NFL games were required to supply team-defense and zero-weight scoring fields; supported public kicking, return and big-play fields were discarded during normalization/admission; prepared production coverage was not rendered on the selected-asset Market or dossier; and a failed source-check timestamp could mark retained facts newly fresh. Current-season facts were not bounded to authoritative completed weeks. Tests cover the actual source/store/preparation/cache and rendered route paths, including a real disposable Sleeper synchronization entry point.
+
+## Contract and correction
+
+Production remains NFLverse NFL player-game evidence joined by the existing authoritative identity resolver. The provider's game record, season, week, provenance and dual clocks survive canonical admission. League coefficients score each observed game independently. Nonzero applicable missing fields withhold the game's fantasy points; a partial known-component subtotal is never a complete game/window. The historical-memory scorer and FOIS formula are unchanged. Unknown player positions do not receive team-defense exemptions. Player special-teams forced fumbles/recoveries remain required when configured.
+
+Only direct provider equivalents are admitted: made kicking/PAT statistics and distance buckets, special-teams touchdowns, return yards, and big-play counts. A 40-yard play is not a 40-yard touchdown. Upper FG buckets combine only when both exist. Missing field-goal/PAT miss semantics remain unknown; explicit attempts equal made permits verified zero misses. No row's absence becomes a zero.
+
+The canonical prepared adapter uses one bounded existing current/prior-season stream and at most two local source-check lookups. For matching regular-season NFL state, windows exclude current/later/unknown-week records beyond week minus one. Explicit historical as-of queries do not borrow today's week. Window denominators are retained game observations, not scheduled weeks or asserted games played. Byes, DNPs and missing weeks are not zero-filled. Complete component scoring does not establish complete season acquisition or final game status.
+
+Old compact caches may expose same-generation top-level sample counts. If scored counts/weeks/reasons were not retained they remain unknown. Newly normalized fields require the next existing legitimate preparation/publication; old discarded source fields are not reconstructed. No new source call, fallback, hydration or expensive preparation occurs merely to display a panel.
+
+Failed/partial source checks retain admitted evidence with explicit qualification, without promoting the check timestamp to successful freshness. League refresh failures are separately disclosed. Prepared source generation is sensitive to adapter version, week boundary and receipt state. Current/prior seasons remain separate; reference scoring/model coefficients and existing numeric averaging are not recalibrated.
+
+## Source evidence and remaining limits
+
+Public authoritative Sleeper league configuration and a bounded 256,000-byte NFLverse schema sample were inspected on November 6, 2026. No private roster payload was exported. Frozen public configurations for Granite one-QB/K/DEF, Arkham Superflex and Day Traders are in tests/fixtures/current_production_leagues.json. In matched offensive fixtures Granite still legitimately lacks player st_ff and st_fum_rec; Day Traders and Arkham require additional unsupported long-TD/bonus evidence. We do not infer those values or claim a live canonical total. This player-game source does not establish team-DEF season production; existing forward K/DEF projections are independent.
+
+## Verification and boundaries
+
+Tests exercise complete/partial/unknown and zero samples, active missing scoring, unknown positions, current versus completed seasons, receipt failure/aging, ownership-independent deduplication, cache serialization/restoration, cross-league rejection and real Market/dossier output. Browser controls use two disposable league scopes and four viewports (320×432, 375×667, 390×844, 1280×900), keyboard focus, touch emulation, no overflow and no disclosure-triggered acquisition. Physical iPhone/Safari and authenticated production recovery are unverified.
+
+Full release validation must pass on the exact final candidate. Original failed attempts remain separate from final evidence. Trade thresholds, Neutral/Custom mathematics, reference valuation formulas, submitted/optimal lineups, league projection scoring, picks, preferences, FOIS provenance, cgroup admission, work reserves and lifecycle controls are preserved. Increased production availability is not proof of a qualified recommendation or better Market accuracy.
